  "Question": "If the quadratic equation obtained by substituting the equation of a line into the equation of an ellipse has 2 distinct real roots, what does this indicate?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "There are 2 intersection points",
    "B": "There are no intersection points",
    "C": "There is 1 intersection point",
    "D": "The line passes through both foci"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Each real root corresponds to the x-coordinate of an intersection point. Therefore, 2 distinct real roots mean there are 2 intersection points.",
